cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark harness, notebooks, or audited telemetry, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Evaluating Symbolic Persona Anchoring and Direct KV-Cache Interventions for Multi-Turn LLM Persona Preservation: A Six-Method, 10-Model Longitudinal Study"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-21"
authors:
  - family-names: "Mehta"
    given-names: "Nabh Sanjay"
    email: "nabhsanjaymehta@phlowerman.com"
    affiliation: "Phlowerman Ventures LLP"
repository-code: "https://github.com/phlowermanventuresllp/kv-cache-vs-spa"
keywords:
  - "Symbolic Persona Anchoring (SPA)"
  - "KV-Cache Steering"
  - "Multi-Turn Persona Preservation"
  - "Activation Steering"
  - "Memory Inception"
  - "Longitudinal LLM Evaluation"
  - "ROPE Positional Alignment"
  - "Inference-Time Control"
abstract: >-
  Extending prior Symbolic Persona Anchoring (SPA) research, this study conducts a balanced
  6x10x4 longitudinal benchmark (240 trajectories, 12,000 turns across 50-turn rollouts)
  across 10 open-weight models (3B-14B) and four personas, comparing baseline controls
  (A1 Raw History, A2 Generic Reminder), symbolic anchoring (A3 Continuous SPA), and
  multi-turn adaptations of direct Key-Value (KV) cache interventions (A4 Belitsky-style
  additive steering, A5 Sun-style mid-layer transplantation, and A6 Memory Inception latent
  KV banks), with SHA-256 checksum verification and bitwise metric recomputation.
